WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.680
- I have to tell you and reiterate

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:04.220
that we are very concerned

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:09.220
by the PRC's provocative
military activity near Taiwan.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.860
- Tension certainly is growing
between China and Taiwan.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.830
And that in turn is prompting a new debate

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:17.520
about whether the US needs
a new policy approach

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.330
to prevent China from
making a move on Taiwan,

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.980
an act that could start
a wider war in Asia

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.560
and between the US and
China, specifically.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.030
- As we've said, the
activity is destabilizing.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.590
It risks miscalculation.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:32.980
And it has the potential

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.470
to undermine regional peace and stability.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:38.010
- China, of course, considers
Taiwan a breakaway province

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.101
that should be made part of China.

00:00:40.101 --> 00:00:44.434
(Jinping speaking foreign language)

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.570
That has been China's
position for a long time,

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.700
though beyond rhetoric,
it hasn't taken steps

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.470
to actually forcibly swallow up Taiwan.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.880
In the last year or so, though,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.840
and particularly in the last few months,

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.720
China has been acting more like a country

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.070
that might use its growing

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.400
and increasingly sophisticated military

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.230
to move on Taiwan and
attempt to force it to unify.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.910
China has sent repeated flights
of its military aircraft

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.920
near Taiwan, including many in areas

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.070
Taiwan considers part of
its air defense perimeter.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.090
So flights have been growing
both larger in number

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.113
and more frequent.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.180
There've also been stepped
up Chinese naval actions,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.160
and recently satellite photos
showed China building up

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:30.520
its three air bases closest to Taiwan.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.230
This obviously concerns Taiwan,

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:35.080
but it's also of direct concern to the US.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.230
In fact, it's caused
some analysts to argue

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.140
that it's time for the US to abandon

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.570
the approach it's taken in
addressing Taiwanese concerns.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:45.410
That approach is called
strategic ambiguity.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.010
Strategic ambiguity means
that while the US provides

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:51.470
military equipment and some
military training to Taiwan,

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.660
it's never said explicitly
whether it would

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.810
or would not come to Taiwan's defense,

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:57.640
if it were attacked by China.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.560
That's been the case for
some four decades now.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.900
The rationale behind strategic ambiguity

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.180
has been that it creates on the one hand

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:08.150
enough fear in China's mind
that an attack on Taiwan

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.640
would bring an American military response,

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.850
that China will be reluctant to move.

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:15.050
While on the other hand, not giving Taiwan

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.230
such a flat assurance America
would come to its rescue,

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.460
that it does something
too bold and reckless

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.493
and brings on the very fight
the US is trying to avoid.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.090
Now, though, some are arguing

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.020
that the time for strategic
ambiguity has ended

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.280
and that the growing threat
from China calls instead

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.970
for strategic clarity.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.530
That is, these voices argue,
the US should make it clear

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.210
that it will come to
Taiwan's defense. Why?

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.240
Well, the argument goes,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.750
China is a different country now

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.240
than it was four decades ago.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.150
It's far stronger militarily

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.780
and much more assertive
in international affairs.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.720
Moreover, US actions in recent years

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.310
in places such as Afghanistan and Syria

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.640
raised doubts internationally
about whether the US

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.560
will stick up for its friends.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.350
Under those circumstances, it's argued,

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.820
China might become reckless

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.960
and miscalculate American resolve

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:05.250
by thinking it can move on
Taiwan without consequence.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.430
And the way to head off
such Chinese thinking

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.950
is to be clear, not ambiguous.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.690
President Biden caused a
diplomatic stir a few days ago

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.840
when he suggested at a town hall meeting

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.260
that he actually is moving
away from strategic ambiguity.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.830
Asked whether the US would
come to Taiwan's defense

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.740
if it were attacked, he said yes,

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.640
there's a commitment to do that.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.960
Later, though, the White House
walked back that comment.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.750
- There is no change in our policy.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.400
Our defense relationship
with Taiwan is guided

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.400
by the Taiwan Relations Act.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.910
- [Gerald] Still, China was quite unhappy

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:36.910
with that Biden comment, which just shows

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.750
that moving away from strategic ambiguity

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.040
to strategic clarity

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.410
would make already tense
relations with China even worse.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.340
And some fear Taiwan would think it has

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.870
a kind of blank check to be as provocative

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.710
with China as it would like.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.670
So put this debate on the
growing list of China issues

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.261
the Biden administration has to tackle.

00:03:56.261 --> 00:03:58.761
(light music)

